invariant: INV-16
file: src/poly1305_wide.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh aead-avx2
reason: the sum's statement, which a gcc build for x86-64 compiles, adds the
  second words with ADD in place of ADC, so the carry out of h0 never
  arrives in h1 and a block whose low half and h0 pass 2^64 loses 2^64 of
  its value. The form in C, which the harnesses and bin/diff_poly1305_wide
  read, is still right. bin/aead_avx2_equiv_test holds the statement to a
  sum in 128-bit arithmetic and the one pass to the two-pass AEAD; the
  script builds it with gcc for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64,
  because no other compiler reads the statement.

--- old
    __asm__("add %[m0], %[h0]\n adc %[m1], %[h1]\n adc %[m2], %[h2]"
--- new
    __asm__("add %[m0], %[h0]\n add %[m1], %[h1]\n adc %[m2], %[h2]"
